Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||05-14-2000||03:50 AM||||i just recently got an '87 gt (selling my 86 SE 2m6, check "the mall!!!!") and noticed tht the "pontiac" on the back does not light up. is it possible that the previous owner disabled them when installing a subwoofer or car alarm? if so, where should i look? if not, any suggestions? one of the reasons i love gt's is that symbol of pontiac pride riding above those noisy flowmastered quad pipes... (btw, 195 for a series 40 flowmaster, with 25 bucks off the labor because the guy who installed it is crazy about fieros. he also drives an 87GT if anyone wants one installed, lemme know!) sorry, i get lost when typing sometimes...<P>THE QUESTION: where should i start looking to find out why the "pontiac" does not light up? thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Uaana||05-14-2000||06:13 AM||||Not to be too obvious but have you tried the bulbs?||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||05-14-2000||10:17 AM||||do you check it with the ignition on or with the ignition off? If the ignition is off, the 'Pontiac' will be off......in other words, if you just turn the lights on but do not turn the ignition on, the 'Pontiac' will not be lit.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroSTETZ||05-14-2000||11:27 AM||||yeah, i tried the bulbs, and the car was running when i did it. i turned on the headlights and got out and went back there, and the running lites were on, but not the pontiac. any info is much appreciated!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Uaana||05-14-2000||12:11 PM||||do you have a line tester? is there power in the lines? I would say if all your fuses are good do a section by section check of the harness.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||05-14-2000||10:56 PM||||On 86 and 87 GT's power for the "PONTIAC" comes from the same power wire as the blower motor in the right hand side of the trunk under the carpet. If someone disconnected the motor or removed it that will break the connection. If it's connected you can check power there too.||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSTETZ||05-14-2000||11:06 PM||||can someone send me pics of possible places to check? i.e. is there a place where the blower motor wire branches off? what fuse controls the blower motor?||||reg||5
Z||000007||BBBAD GT||06-12-2000||10:57 PM||||I just checked mine, and my 'PONTIAC' letter are lit up when the motor is on period.  It stays on if the lights are on or off.  Is this normal?  I don't see any GT's around me to check.  I would suspect it would come on when the lights are on, not just the motor.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||tgowens||06-12-2000||11:12 PM||||ok - here's the deal -- 'PONTIAC' will be on when the ignition is on whether the motor is running or not. it should be off under any other condition, i.e. park lights on and ignition off = no 'PONTIAC' -- headlights on and ignition off - no 'PONTIAC' -- motor running (or not) with the ignition in the "on" position = yes 'PONTIAC' -- ignition in the 'acc' position = no 'PONTIAC'<P>I think I covered all the situations - oh yes - ignition off and keys in pocket = no 'PONTIAC'..........<P>the wierd thing about it is that we rarely see the 'PONTIAC' unless we are following another Fiero or we back up to a plate glass window............I have an '87GT and I just went out and did all this checkin'......it was kinda nice to see my 'PONTIAC' all lit up (but now I know that I have a taillight out unless I tap the light in which case it comes back on -- sheesh, I hate abuse!!)||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula||06-13-2000||09:31 AM||||what if the motor is on and the ignition is off?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bill Osmer||06-13-2000||10:15 AM||||Still didn't hear the answer to the question: have you checked the lamps??<P>When I 1st got my GT, there were over 13 burned out lamps all over the car, including all of the "PONTIAC" bulbs. To check, just remove one of the tailight housings, twist out the bulb socket and look at the bulb - if it's burned out, it's probably black. Replace with new one and test - you'll see right away if that's your problem source.||||reg||5
Z||000011||tgowens||06-13-2000||11:11 AM||||Well Bill, I think BBBADGT said his 'PONTIAC' was lit so I would assume that the lamps were good...........<P>Formula, only you would ask that question -- actually if the motor is on and the ignition is off (which is a condition only found on Formulas in Waynesburg, PA) the 'PONTIAC' lights on and off and on and off and on and off................makes it a big hit at Christmas time........oh, and it lights up in yellow - I forgot that part.......||||reg||1
Z||000012||BBBAD GT||06-13-2000||01:33 PM||||Ummm, I don't have a problem with my Pontiac light, just wondering why its lit up when I don't have the lights on and the car running.  Just seemed weird to me.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||FieroSTETZ||06-14-2000||12:34 PM||||discovered what had happened: the previous owner had disconnected the pontiac to get power for the viper alarm- i disconnected the alarm, connected  the loose lead that was sitting next to it, turend on the ignition and the pontiac came on- thanks for all the help! as for the overheating mentioned in my other posts, i am going on friday to have it looked at (radiator and water pump) i dont wanna just start swapping parts. how hard is it to install a radiator? since no one wants to buy my 86SE i figure i will just have to strip it for parts and call ecology. maybe i can just get the radiator from there||||reg||1
Z||000014||dogtired||06-14-2000||12:37 PM||||Probably isn't this but there is a common ground connector/screw right above the right rear tire. You have to remove the fender well to get to it???<BR>Just a thought  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and I have so FEW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||6
